In the highly competitive e-commerce landscape, the quality of user experience (UX) and customer support play a vital role in a platform’s success. One of the most valuable sources of data for evaluating these two aspects is direct consumer feedback recorded on review pages in the Play Store and App Store. Unfortunately, manually processing and analyzing tens of thousands of comments is too time-consuming and highly impractical. Yet, the Product Manager and Customer Service teams are required to act quickly in detecting critical issues, such as identifying the main causes of customer dissatisfaction during a specific period or finding technical issues (bugs) in the latest app update.
In response to these challenges, this project was initiated to design and develop an Interactive Dashboard as a data-driven analytics solution. This system aims to automate the process of extracting insights from raw user review data into actionable information. Through this dashboard, shifts in customer sentiment trends can be clearly visualized, while also facilitating a more specific analysis of issues or complaints based on feature categories or app versions, enabling internal teams to formulate improvements more quickly and effectively.
